# Unreleased
- Breaking: an element that sets the `children` prop and also has nested
  children is now a syntax error, for example `<Foo children>a</Foo>` and
  `<Foo children=x>...xs</Foo>`. Before, mlx dropped the nested children
  silently. `<Foo children />` and `<Foo children></Foo>` are still valid.

# 0.12
- Add JSX fragments: `<></>`, `<>a b</>` and `<>...xs</>`. A fragment lowers to
  a list expression with the `[@JSX]` attribute, and `<>...xs</>` lowers to `xs`
  with `[@JSX]`. A fragment used as a function argument needs parentheses:
  `f (<>a</>)`.
- `</>` stays a valid operator, like `<>`, for example `let (</>) a b = a`.
  Inside a fragment, parenthesize it: `<>(a </> b)</>`.
- Breaking: operators that start with `<>` followed by `<` or `...`, `</>`
  followed by `<`, or `>...` (for example `<><`, `<><=`, `>...`) are now split
  and no longer parse as one operator.
- Add JSX children spread: `<Foo> ...expr </Foo>` passes `expr` directly as
  `~children:expr`. The spread must be the only child.
  [#45](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/45)
- Fix JSX elements closed directly before `|]` and `}`, such as
  `[|<div>a</div>|]`. [#46](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/46)
- Restore unparenthesized expressions in object overrides while keeping JSX
  closing tags valid directly before record and indexing braces.
  [#47](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/47)
- Accept quoted strings with an empty delimiter, `{|...|}`.
  [#37](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/issues/37)
- Fix duplicate `children` labels when a JSX element sets `children`
  explicitly. [#36](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/36)
- Support OCaml 5.5: the vendored OCaml parser is 5.5.0 and ocamlmerlin-mlx
  uses merlin 5.8.1-505. mlx still builds with OCaml 4.14 and later.
- Add Emacs mlx-mode to the editor support list.
  [#33](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/33)

# 0.11
- Support for OCaml 5.4 [#22](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/22)
- Fix windows [#20](https://github.com/ocaml-mlx/mlx/pull/20)

# 0.10
- compatibility with OCaml 5.3

# 0.9
- initial version
